Our collaboration with the U.S. Customs and Border Protection (CBP) has been pivotal in reducing customs clearance times by 10% over the last quarter. We attribute this improvement to the implementation of the Automated Commercial Environment (ACE) system, which has facilitated real-time data exchange between our operations team and customs officials.

Moreover, our partnership with the vessel scheduling software provided by SeaTrack Systems has enabled us to optimize berthing schedules, leading to a 5% increase in vessel turnaround efficiency. This system allows for better coordination between our terminal operations and shipping lines, including Pacific Shipping Co., which frequently utilizes our ports for their trans-Pacific routes.

Looking ahead, we are targeting a further reduction in customs clearance times to an average of 10 hours by Q1 2024 through additional training for our staff and enhanced integration with the ACE system. Continuous monitoring of vessel scheduling efficiency will also be conducted to ensure we maximize our terminal capacity and improve service delivery to our clients, particularly those relying on just-in-time logistics.

**Action Items:**
1. Increase training sessions for staff on ACE system utilization.
2. Conduct weekly meetings with CBP representatives to address any emerging customs issues.
3. Evaluate the performance of SeaTrack Systems to identify potential software upgrades.

By focusing on these strategic areas, Harbor Logistics Solutions aims to enhance operational efficiency and maintain our competitive edge in the cargo handling sector.